1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,600
I'm your China Travel Expert.
我是你的中国旅游专家

2
00:00:01,600 --> 00:00:04,000
Seven in ten old Shanghainese lived here.
旧时七成上海人都住这儿

3
00:00:04,000 --> 00:00:06,300
Behind one stone gate — shikumen.
就在这道石库门后

4
00:00:06,300 --> 00:00:08,600
These lanes are called longtang.
这些弄堂·上海的巷子

5
00:00:08,600 --> 00:00:11,000
Laundry poles turn the sky to a canopy.
晾衣杆撑起一片天

6
00:00:11,000 --> 00:00:13,300
Breakfast stalls fire up before dawn.
天没亮·早餐摊就开火

7
00:00:13,300 --> 00:00:15,600
Neighbors gossip on stools — 嘎三胡.
邻居坐着嘎三胡·唠家常

8
00:00:15,600 --> 00:00:18,000
Built in the 1850s: Western frame, Chinese heart.
始于1850年代·西式骨中式魂

9
00:00:18,000 --> 00:00:20,300
This is everyday Shanghai — not the skyline.
这才是上海日常·不是天际线

10
00:00:20,300 --> 00:00:23,200
★ Expert Tip: Come 7am, the lane wakes with breakfast, not tourists.
内行提示：早7点来·弄堂醒于早餐

11
00:00:23,200 --> 00:00:26,000
Soup dumplings or scallion pancake first?
先吃小笼还是葱油饼？评论区见
